    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3019" root="بَقَلَ" body-key="b">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بقّل</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَبْقِيِلٌ</span>, <i>He</i> (a pastor) <i>left</i> camels
<i>to pasture upon</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَقْل</span> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And, [hence,
app.,] inf. n. as above, <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَاسَ</span> (Sgh, K.) You
say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بقّل الدَّايَّةَ</span>, i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَاسَهَا</span>, meaning <i>He tended,</i> or
<i>took care of, the beast well.</i> (TK.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also 1.

